  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/034-records-bridge-decision.md` exists, names the chosen F-c option with rationale, and — if records are included — states explicitly that they come from a text-seeded `/api/ai/search/records` query rather than document-content vector similarity. It was written before the implementation commit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given more similar documents than one page holds, when the user scrolls to the bottom of the results list, then the next page loads automatically and rows accumulate in the same list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (ADR-051): the rendered Find tab contains no numbered page link, no prev/next control, no chevron next-page button and no "Load more" button — asserted by an automated test over the rendered output, not by inspection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the results list does not load the entire result set in one page to avoid paging — page size is bounded and `hasMore` reflects reality.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the results scroll container overflows, when it renders, then it carries the locally recreated thin scrollbar style, and `src/client/office-addins/package.json` still lists `@spaarke/auth` as its only Spaarke dependency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an indexed document with no permitted similar documents, when Find renders, then an explicit empty state is shown and announced — not an indefinite spinner.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the visualization response includes parent hub nodes, when results render, then those nodes are omitted or labeled distinctly from similarity matches — never presented as content matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All results come from the per-row-authorized surface delivered by task 032 — verified by grep that no unhardened similarity route is called from the add-in.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All six `&lt;ui-tests&gt;` pass, including the dark-mode and keyboard/announcement checks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean and `npm run build` succeeds in `src/client/office-addins`; all unit tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If any BFF file changed, publish size was measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive` and both absolute sizes, delta and tool are recorded; if the task is client-only, the PR says so explicitly.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-16 + NFR-05; plan.md §3 finding F-c. The bridge decision is the load-bearing output of this task — a future reader must be able to tell, from `notes/`, whether a record in the Find list was a vector match, a hub node, or a text query hit.
  </notes>

